================================================================================
Run:      2026-10-09 20:07:56-20:17:51 NZDT (device clock: NZ local time labelled UTC,
          `no clock timezone`, ~2 s behind tb470; DUT times below are therefore NZDT)
Bench:    tb470, console u0 (DUT only); Test Engineer terrenceb@terrenceb-dl
Tester:   bench-runner (by hand: tools/tb ckcon / ckyn / ckreload, tools/rcdiff.py,
          tools/rc2cfg.py; no framework script)
Graded:   tester
Case:     AWPTCM-T47114 (Draft), objective (empty). The case has 1 step in the test-case
          database, with empty text and expected result. Steps A-D below are the tester's
          procedure, built from the title and the AW+ x230 `crypto secure-mode` command page
          ("Use this command to put the device into Secure Mode"; mode Global Configuration;
          `show secure-mode` answers "Secure mode is enabled"), 4 steps
Build:    swi_f awplus_main-20261008-57 (x230v2_28GS-awplus_main-20261008-57.rel, build date
          Thu Oct 8 00:10:09 UTC 2026), bootloader 6.2.40
Configs:  swi_f.cfg (running-config after setup, before step A; saved to startup: yes, by
          step C's `write`, which added `crypto secure-mode` to it)

VERDICT: PASS -- `crypto secure-mode` + write + reload (265 s): the x230 booted into secure mode
      precondition ......................... PASS  (`show secure-mode`: "Secure mode is disabled")
      crypto secure-mode accepted .......... PASS  (advisory "% Save the config and restart ...";
                                                    `crypto secure-mode` in running-config)
      write + reload ....................... PASS  (startup carries it; login seen after 265 s)
      boot into secure mode ................ PASS  (boot: "Creating secure mode hostkey"; log
                                                    20:16:04 "crypto secure-mode enabled"; after
                                                    boot "Secure mode is enabled")
      SSH server algorithm sets ............ changed (CBC/CTR ciphers, ECDH-nistp KEX,
                                                    hmac-sha2-256, ecdsa hostkeys only)
      exception log / boot config .......... None / flash:/default.cfg (file exists), unchanged
CAVEAT:  Release verification was not part of the case. The same boot printed "Please verify
         release with the 'crypto verify' command" and logged, at 20:16:04, `user.warning ...
         Verification of the release file has failed, please verify it.` (STEP C, STEP D). No
         `crypto verify` pair was configured or tried.
         `show secure-mode` already read "Secure mode is enabled" after step B, before the save
         and reload (STEP B), so it reports the configured state. The proof that the unit BOOTED
         into secure mode is the boot's "Creating secure mode hostkey" line, the 20:16:04 log line
         and the changed SSH algorithm sets after the reload. The "Secure mode setup" / "FIPS
         Provider Install" / "Secure mode enable" boot jobs are not graded as proof on their own.
         The SSH algorithm sets were not read between step B and the reload.
         The features secure mode disables (Telnet, SSHv1, SNMPv1/v2, privilege levels, weak
         algorithms) were not exercised one by one: Telnet and the SSH server were already
         disabled before step A.

